    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented for owner-identity version 2.\n\n## Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed inside identifiers only)\nAdded a shared `Owner.IDENTIFIER_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and folded it into each identifier so every one changes and no V1 value can recur, while leaving user-facing region values plain:\n\n- **`regionCode()`** (`Owner.java`): now `\"V2\" + region` \u2192 the `<REGION>` component of the `memberId` becomes e.g. `V2NSW273C1A9F2B4`. `getFiscalYear()` still reads the FY from the tail, so it's unaffected by the longer prefix.\n- **`identityKeyMaterial()`** (`Owner.java`): now hashes `\"V2|\" + telephone|email|soundex`. Because the tag is a constant shared by every owner, hard/soft duplicate detection is unchanged.\n- **`householdId(...)`** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): now hashes `\"V2|\" + normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`, so household grouping is preserved.\n- **`locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's region** are untouched \u2014 they read `getRegion()`/`getLocality()` (plain `NSW`), so the `V2` tag never leaks into them.\n\n## Response shape\nIn `openapi.yml`: removed top-level `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`, added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping the three, an `identity: $ref` on `Owner`, and a top-level integer `apiVersion` (example 2). Request fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged. The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` now sets `apiVersion` to the constant `2` and populates `identity.{memberId,identityKey,householdId}`.\n\n## Audit schema v2\n`OwnerCreatedEvent` now carries `schemaVersion = 2` and a recomputed `ownerSegment` (from the owner's V2 identity), emitted as e.g. `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
