    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence of validations and side-effects applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner(...)`.\n\n## Validations (in order, each failure aborts)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must be `OWNER_ADMIN` before the body runs.\n\n2. **JSON deserialization / enum check** \u2014 Body bound to `OwnerFieldsDto`; the `title` enum is validated by Jackson's `@JsonCreator`.\n\n3. **Bean Validation of the request DTO** (`@Valid` + interface `@Validated`) \u2014 runs before the controller body; failure \u2192 **400**:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`: `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n\n4. **`normalizeAndValidate(owner)`** \u2014 after MapStruct mapping (`id` and `pets` ignored; email lower-cased on set). In order, each \u2192 **400**:\n   - Address normalization must succeed (via `AddressNormalizer`: trim/collapse/upper-case/expand ST\u00b7RD\u00b7AVE).\n   - Telephone must convert to E.164 (`toE164`); invalid \u2192 400, else stored normalized.\n   - Email must **not** be a disposable domain (`isDisposableEmail`).\n   - `owner.isPostcodeValid()` must pass.\n   - `registrationDate`, if present, must not be in the future.\n\n5. **Daily limit** \u2014 `isDailyLimitReached(registrationDate)` (\u2265100 registrations that day) \u2192 **429**.\n\n6. **`checkForConflicts(owner)`** (after household is assigned):\n   - `isDuplicateIdentity(owner)` (identity-key match) \u2192 **409**.\n   - `isCityAtCapacity(city)` (\u226550 owners in city) \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Side-effects / mutations (in order, on the successful path)\n\n7. **`normalizeAndValidate` mutations** \u2014 sets normalized address, sets E.164 telephone, and rolls `registrationDate` to a business day (`toBusinessDay`; defaults to today if null).\n\n8. **`assignHousehold(owner)`** \u2014 computes and sets `householdId` (runs *before* conflict checks; feeds household size + membership level).\n\n9. **`assignDerivedAttributes(owner, sharesHousehold)`** \u2014 sets, in order: `memberId`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `householdSize`, `membershipLevel`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (via `assignPossibleDuplicate`), and `riskFlag`.\n\n10. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` in a `@Transactional` write. Generates the identity `id`. `pets` has `cascade = ALL` but is empty on create, so nothing cascades. (No `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks exist.)\n\n11. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... memberId=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")`.\n\n12. **\"Owner created event\"** \u2014 `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)`: serializes an `OwnerCreatedEvent` record to JSON and writes it to the `AUDIT` logger. (This is a log line, **not** a Spring `ApplicationEvent` \u2014 there is no `publishEvent`/`@EventListener` anywhere.)\n\n13. **Welcome notification** \u2014 `enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner)`: writes to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n14. **Response** \u2014 `created(owner)` \u2192 **201** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and an `OwnerDto` body (`apiVersion=2`, nested identity).\n\n## Cross-cutting notes\n\n- **Idempotency wrapper**: `addOwner` (before `createOwner`) checks an `Idempotency-Key` header; a replayed key returns the previously-created owner as **200** and short-circuits everything below. On a successful 201, the new id is recorded against the key.\n- **No validation groups**, **no `@InitBinder`**, **no entity lifecycle callbacks**. The custom validator in the repo (`PetAgeValidator`) applies to **Pets only** and is not part of this flow.\n- The controller method itself is **not `@Transactional`**; the many read helpers and the single write each run in their own transaction (`saveOwner` read-write, finders read-only).\n- Business rejections are all `RejectedRequestException(HttpStatus)`, translated to the exact status (400/409/429) by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\nNothing was modified."
